mory, or I/O resources to deliver the same level of service, which increases energy consumption. Proper indexing, good data modeling, and regular maintenance help reduce unnecessary resource use."},{"v":"💡 Improvement potential identified"},{"v":"The criterion is met if a strategy is applied to optimize database performance."},{"v":"Significant"},null,{"v":1.0,"f":"1"},{"v":1.5,"f":"1,5"},{"v":1.5,"f":"1,5"},null,{"v":null}]},{"c":[null,{"v":"Date(2025,2,4)","f":"4.3"},{"v":"Does the product use database/storage technologies suited to the intended uses?"},{"v":"If the product\u0027s storage needs are large, it may be worth specializing storage technologies:\n- PG/MYSQL/Oracle/SQLServer or object-relational\n- MongoDB for document-oriented use.\n- Column-oriented database for analytics.\n- Specialized database (vector, time series)."},{"v":"✅ Confirmed strength"},{"v":"Improvement potential exists if the project does not use elasticity tools (auto-scaling) and the load is not constant.\nThe project has specific storage needs that would be better served by another storage system, and the volume is large (\u003e several hundred GB)."},{"v":"Significant"},null,{"v":0.0,"f":"0"},{"v":1.5,"f":"1,5"},{"v":0.0,"f":"0"},null,{"v":null}]},{"c":[null,{"v":"Date(2025,3,4)","f":"4.4"},{"v":"Are test databases as large as production databases?"},{"v":"In general, there is no need to have as much data in test environments as in production."},{"v":"💡 Improvement potential identified"},{"v":"Improvement potential exists if some test databases are as large as production databases."},{"v":"Significant"},null,{"v":1.0,"f":"1"},{"v":1.5,"f":"1,5"},{"v":1.5,"f":"1,5"},null,{"v":null}]},{"c":[null,{"v":"Date(2025,4,4)","f":"4.5"},{"v":"Is there duplicated data?"},{"v":"If data is duplicated and this is not part of the product\u0027s high-availability strategy, it generally indicates an optimization opportunity — unless the duplication results from intentional denormalization for performan